WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.923
<v Ken Watanabe>Alright, it’s 10:02, let’s get started. Thanks for joining, everyone. Quick round of updates before we dive in?</v>

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:21.294
<v Nadia Petrova>Sure, I’ll go first. Sales Ops is still working through the Q2 pipeline cleanup, but nothing blocking. Oh, and the new dashboard is live, if anyone wants a peek.</v>

00:00:22.029 --> 00:00:33.183
<v Ethan Brooks>Nice. Deal Desk is mostly steady. We had a couple weird escalations last week, but I think those are sorted. I’ll ping you, Nadia, about one of them after.</v>

00:00:34.254 --> 00:00:43.100
<v Julia Costa>Billing’s been quiet, honestly. Just prepping for the end-of-month close. I did get a couple partner questions about renewal invoices, but nothing urgent.</v>

00:00:44.256 --> 00:00:51.948
<v Ken Watanabe>Good to hear. I’m mostly heads down on the new partner onboarding flow. We’re seeing fewer errors, so that’s promising.</v>

00:00:52.471 --> 00:00:59.009
<v Nadia Petrova>Oh, and I’ll be out next Friday, just FYI. But I’ll make sure anything urgent is covered.</v>

00:00:59.416 --> 00:01:02.493
<v Ethan Brooks>Thanks, Nadia. I think that’s it for updates?</v>

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:15.528
<v Ken Watanabe>Yep, let’s move to the main item. So, we need to finalize the changes to the Ecosystem Ops logic and definitions. Everyone had a chance to review the doc I sent?</v>

00:01:16.225 --> 00:01:25.456
<v Julia Costa>Yeah, I went through it. The renewal logic is clearer now, but I have a question on how we’re pulling the oldest Closed-Won opp.</v>

00:01:25.706 --> 00:01:34.937
<v Ethan Brooks>Same, actually. So for renewals, we’re not copying from the source opp anymore, right? We’re looking at the account’s first Closed-Won, New Business opp?</v>

00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:46.133
<v Ken Watanabe>Exactly. That’s the main change. The Initial Source for renewals will always reference the oldest Closed-Won, New Biz opp on the account, not the linked source opp.</v>

00:01:46.593 --> 00:01:56.977
<v Nadia Petrova>Just to clarify, that means if the oldest opp was PQL, but the renewal’s source opp was AE Generated, the renewal still shows PQL as Initial Source?</v>

00:01:58.371 --> 00:02:04.525
<v Ken Watanabe>Correct. It’s a little counterintuitive, but it’s what aligns with how we want to track attribution.</v>

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:11.718
<v Julia Costa>Okay, but what if there’s no Closed-Won, New Biz opp? Like, if the account only has renewals?</v>

00:02:12.985 --> 00:02:19.908
<v Ethan Brooks>Good catch. I think in that case, Initial Source would just be blank, or maybe default to Unknown?</v>

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:32.395
<v Ken Watanabe>Yeah, that’s rare, but it can happen. I’d say we default to Unknown if there’s no Closed-Won, New Biz opp. I’ll add that as a note for edge cases.</v>

00:02:32.884 --> 00:02:37.115
<v Nadia Petrova>Sounds good. I’ll make sure that’s clear in the handbook update.</v>

00:02:38.173 --> 00:02:40.866
<v Julia Costa>Thanks. Otherwise, I’m good with the changes.</v>

00:02:41.584 --> 00:02:48.891
<v Ethan Brooks>Same here. The table in the Use Cases section is a lot easier to follow now, by the way.</v>

00:02:49.453 --> 00:02:52.915
<v Ken Watanabe>Great. Any other concerns before we lock this in?</v>

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:58.974
<v Nadia Petrova>Nope, I’m good. I’ll take the action to update the handbook page within two weeks.</v>

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:10.180
<v Ken Watanabe>Perfect. So, to recap: we’re updating the Default Logic, Definitions, and Use Cases sections as discussed, including the new renewal logic. Nadia will update the handbook.</v>

00:03:10.836 --> 00:03:13.144
<v Julia Costa>Awesome. Thanks for driving this, Ken.</v>

00:03:14.006 --> 00:03:18.237
<v Ethan Brooks>Yeah, thanks. Should make things a lot clearer for the field.</v>

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:29.320
<v Ken Watanabe>Alright, last thing—quick unrelated item. We got the results from the vendor satisfaction survey. Overall, pretty positive, but there were a few comments about response times.</v>

00:03:30.617 --> 00:03:34.079
<v Nadia Petrova>Was that mostly about support tickets, or onboarding stuff?</v>

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:43.171
<v Ken Watanabe>Mostly support tickets. I’ll send the summary around, but I think we should do a quick review of our SLAs next week.</v>

00:03:43.407 --> 00:03:47.637
<v Julia Costa>I can pull the last quarter’s ticket data if that helps.</v>

00:03:48.977 --> 00:03:52.824
<v Ken Watanabe>That’d be great, Julia. Can you send it by Tuesday?</v>

00:03:53.363 --> 00:03:54.863
<v Julia Costa>Yep, will do.</v>

00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:57.356
<v Ethan Brooks>Anything else for today?</v>

00:03:58.835 --> 00:04:00.335
<v Nadia Petrova>Not from me.</v>

00:04:00.585 --> 00:04:07.508
<v Ken Watanabe>Alright, thanks everyone. Nadia, let me know if you need anything for the handbook update. Otherwise, we’re good.</v>

00:04:08.483 --> 00:04:11.176
<v Nadia Petrova>Will do. Have a good one, all.</v>

00:04:11.825 --> 00:04:13.325
<v Julia Costa>Bye!</v>

00:04:14.547 --> 00:04:16.047
<v Ethan Brooks>See ya.</v>

00:04:16.815 --> 00:04:18.353
<v Ken Watanabe>Thanks, everyone. Talk soon.</v>
